{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/comparison-summary.test.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/summarize-assistants.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/render-comparison-table.mjs benchmark/fixtures/T3-comparison-summary/student-tests.mjs'","aggregated_output":"import assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport test from \"node:test\";\n\nimport { renderComparisonTable } from \"./render-comparison-table.mjs\";\nimport { summarizeAssistants } from \"./summarize-assistants.mjs\";\n\ntest(\"summarizes eligible runs by assistant in stable order\", () => {\n  const runs = Object.freeze([\n    Object.freeze({\n      run_id: \"codex-slow\",\n      assistant: \"Codex\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      score: 91,\n      elapsed_ms: 2_000,\n    }),\n    Object.freeze({\n      run_id: \"claude-best\",\n      assistant: \"Claude Code\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      score: 96,\n      elapsed_ms: 1_250,\n      comparison_eligible: true,\n    }),\n    Object.freeze({\n      run_id: \"codex-best\",\n      assistant: \"Codex\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      score: 95,\n      elapsed_ms: 1_000,\n    }),\n    Object.freeze({\n      run_id: \"failed-run\",\n      assistant: \"Claude Code\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"fail\",\n      score: 100,\n      elapsed_ms: 10,\n    }),\n    Object.freeze({\n      run_id: \"excluded-run\",\n      assistant: \"Codex\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      comparison_eligible: false,\n      score: 100,\n      elapsed_ms: 10,\n    }),\n  ]);\n\n  assert.deepEqual(summarizeAssistants(runs), [\n    {\n      assistant: \"Claude Code\",\n      run_count: 1,\n      best_score: 96,\n      best_run_id: \"claude-best\",\n      median_elapsed_ms: 1_250,\n    },\n    {\n      assistant: \"Codex\",\n      run_count: 2,\n      best_score: 95,\n      best_run_id: \"codex-best\",\n      median_elapsed_ms: 1_500,\n    },\n  ]);\n});\n\ntest(\"breaks a best-score tie with elapsed time\", () => {\n  const runs = [\n    {\n      run_id: \"slower\",\n      assistant: \"OpenCode\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      score: 94,\n      elapsed_ms: 1_100,\n    },\n    {\n      run_id: \"faster\",\n      assistant: \"OpenCode\",\n      status: \"complete\",\n      acceptance_status: \"pass\",\n      score: 94,\n      elapsed_ms: 900,\n    },\n  ];\n\n  assert.equal(summarizeAssistants(runs)[0].best_run_id, \"faster\");\n});\n\ntest(\"renders the exact Markdown table format\", () => {\n  const summaries = [\n    {\n      assistant: \"Open|Code\",\n      run_count: 2,\n      best_score: 95.5,\n      best_run_id: \"run|2\",\n      median_elapsed_ms: 1_250,\n    },\n  ];\n\n  assert.equal(\n    renderComparisonTable(summaries),\n    [\n      \"| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |\",\n      \"|---|---:|---:|---|---:|\",\n      \"| Open\\\\|Code | 2 | 95.5 | run\\\\|2 | 1.250 s |\",\n    ].join(\"\\n\"),\n  );\n});\n\ntest(\"renders an explicit empty state below the table header\", () => {\n  assert.equal(\n    renderComparisonTable([]),\n    [\n      \"| Assistant | Runs | Best score | Best run | Median time |\",\n      \"|---|---:|---:|---|---:|\",\n      \"\",\n      \"_No eligible runs._\",\n    ].join(\"\\n\"),\n  );\n});\n/**\n * Build one comparison summary per assistant from raw benchmark run records.\n */\nexport function summarizeAssistants(runs) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(runs)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"runs must be an array\");\n  }\n\n  return [];\n}\n/**\n * Render assistant summaries as a stable Markdown table.\n */\nexport function renderComparisonTable(summaries) {\n  if (!Array.isArray(summaries)) {\n    throw new TypeError(\"summaries must be an array\");\n  }\n\n  return \"\";\n}\n// Add at least two meaningful node:test cases for the feature contract.\n// Do not copy or modify the committed comparison-summary.test.mjs suite.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"reasoning","text":"Need implement. Let's understand contract precisely. summarizeAssistants:\n1. !Array -> TypeError\n2. Eligible if status === \"complete\", acceptance_status === \"pass\", and comparison_eligible !== false. Note comparison_eligible true or undefined? The suite passes true and undefined. Exclude only false.\n3. Validate eligible runs: run_id and assistant must be non-empty strings; score finite number 0-100; elapsed_ms finite >=0. Throw TypeError for invalid eligible data. Ineligible runs invalid fields don't matter. Need validate before grouping? Yes. We need decide order of validation vs eligibility. For eligible runs, if invalid throw TypeError. We must not mutate input.\nPotential tricky: NaN/infinity check. Use Number.isFinite. Non-empty strings means typeof string and length > 0. score must be finite number from 0 through 100 inclusive. elapsed_ms finite >= 0.\n4. Group by exact case-sensitive assistant.\n5. Return object with assistant, run_count, best_score, best_run_id, median_elapsed_ms.\n6. best run highest score, tie lower elapsed time, then lexicographically smaller run_id using JS string comparison. Need be careful if run_id maybe not string? But validation ensures non-empty string. Comparison with localeCompare? contract says normal JavaScript string comparison, which for > or < lexicographic. Use < >.\n7. median: sort numeric. For even count average two middle values. If count odd, middle. Need median of all eligible runs for assistant. Values are elapsed_ms (number). For even average maybe .5. Return number. Use sort by numeric, maybe not stable? Median unaffected.\n8. Sort summaries by assistant string. Do not mutate input.\nReturn array.\n\nrenderComparisonTable:\n1. TypeError if summaries not array or summary invalid fields. assistant and best_run_id non-empty strings; run_count positive integer; best_score finite 0-100; median_elapsed_ms finite >=0.\nNeed positive integer means >0 and Number.isInteger. \"run_count must be a positive integer\". Could use Number.isInteger and >0.\nPreserve order.\nExact header line as given. Then separator. Then for each summary: `| {assistant escaped} | {run_count} | {best_score} | {best_run_id escaped} | {seconds formatted} s |` Need ensure best_score rendered as original number? Contract says return exact header, render median as seconds with exactly 3 decimals. It doesn't specify formatting of best_score. In test, 95.5 rendered as \"95.5\". Just toString. For integer 95 would render \"95\". Need maybe Number(value) toString. But validation finite; it can be e.g. 95.0, toString \"95\". Is that okay? Probably.\nEscape | as \\|. Use replaceAll('|', '\\\\|').\nMedian seconds: (ms/1000).toFixed(3). e.g. 1250 -> 1.250. 0 -> 0.000. Note if median has fractional ms, toFixed.\nEmpty array: header, blank line, `_No eligible runs._`.\n\nNeed add tests. Need at least two meaningful tests. We can add more. Need import modules. We need test ineligible runs with invalid fields, tie-breaking lexicographically, validation errors, render invalid summary, median even/odd. But at least two real. Let's cover edge cases: \n- ineligible runs skipped and invalid fields ignored (e.g. status != complete, missing score etc.)\n- tie-breaking by run_id when scores and elapsed equal.\n- render escapes and empty.\nMaybe compare summary.\n\nLet's write code with apply_patch? Need use apply_patch. But no apply_patch tool in current tools list. Wait system says use apply_patch tool but only tools provided are exec_command, write_stdin, list_mcp_resources, etc. There is no apply_patch. Hmm. The system instruction says \"Emit function calls to run terminal commands and apply patches... Use apply_patch tool\". But tools available do not include apply_patch. In Codex CLI typical there is apply_patch tool. It might be omitted. Need use exec_command to write files. But we can use cat or echo? Better use exec_command with heredoc or printf. We can edit files using shell redirection. Since cwd has write permission. Use `cat > file` via exec_command. Need ensure no apply_patch. We'll use exec_command to write whole files."}}
